title The number compared, not copied -- Tablecloth's first Glow desk, and a guard that lets an honest raise through
prompt The standing Silence seat: open on ListAgents and the cold roster, reds first, then the infrastructure half of Grain in Glow -- the vanes and services.
think Silence now runs from grain-silence, its own clone, born tonight by tools/l/birth_a_clone.rish. That closes the %291 shared-checkout class on this bench structurally, which was the older of the two doors my last lap left standing; the other, %328's seat, stays a design question rather than a lap.
think Reds first read clean -- construction/REDS.md holds one row and zero OPEN, so the constructive queue was genuinely open. The cold roster ran 94 guards to 89 green, 5 red, tree_moved=no: rule_twin is gate %7, width_check is another body's, two Pond rows are Hush's, and remember_git_nib was only the card's nib lagging HEAD, which this round's own commit closes.
think Surveying my lane's rooms found the gap by counting rather than by memory. Every infrastructure vane carrying a bound worth naming already stands in src/shape/ -- Aurora four pedestals, Mantra four, Caravan three, Tally six, Comlink one -- and Tablecloth, which the Brix-facing manifest and the four comlink/guest_tablecloth_query_* wires both lean on, stood there with zero Glow desks of any kind.
think Reading the elder Tend witnesses before copying them found the fault worth fixing. tools/ca/caravan_glow_tend_limb3_witness.rish greps for the literal 48 in the desk AND for `max_name_len: u32 = 48` in the Rye, which writes the value a third time inside the guard: raise that bound honestly in both real rooms and the guard still reds until a hand edits the witness too. A guard that reds on correct work is a guard someone turns off.
think So the new scan carries no value of its own. tools/fixtures/t/tablecloth_glow_tend_scan.sh reads the number the pedestal shows and the number brushstroke/tablecloth.rye publishes as max_artifacts, and compares them -- with placard_order, citation, desk_example and rye_max_artifacts as its four readings and one verdict line.
obs The control proves the design rather than only the guard. Ten cases in a throwaway pen: eight refusals (desk moved alone, rye moved alone, a placard line dropped, the placard reordered, the citation stripped, either file absent, the bound unpublished) and two welcomes -- the tree as written, and a bound raised to 64 in BOTH rooms walking free. That second welcome is the whole difference from the elder shape, so it is asserted as hard as any refusal.
obs I graded src/shape/README.md at --service 3 when the card scores service 0-100, and read the resulting C as the page's. Judged honestly on the card's four questions -- named by the card, 418 living citers, current as of this touch, carried in the seed -- it reads 95 and the page lands A (94). A judged input handed in carelessly is indistinguishable from a measurement until someone reads the scale.
obs The roster row takes tier cadence, matching the six Glow witnesses beside it, because the metal leg builds through the Zig toolchain; the pure scan and control together run in under a second, so a hand asking for the guard by name pays almost nothing.
loom witness=tablecloth_glow_tend verdict=GREEN scan_verdict=agree control_welcomes=2 control_refusals=8 control_wrong=0 metal=EXIT:0
loom roster=cold guards_run=94 guards_green=89 guards_red=5 tree_moved=no
loom roster_rows=112->113 tier_cadence=18->19
file src/shape/shape-tablecloth-catalog-capacity.glow the vane's first Glow desk, naming max_artifacts beside its source
file tools/fixtures/t/tablecloth_glow_tend_scan.sh the drift reading -- both numbers read, neither remembered
file tools/fixtures/t/tablecloth_glow_tend_control.sh ten cases in a pen, eight refusals and two welcomes
file tools/t/tablecloth_glow_tend_witness.rish the rung: scan, control, then lower-build-run on metal
file construction/standing-equipment.kyri the guard takes its seat at tier cadence
file src/shape/README.md the museum's roster and its own stamp move together
file construction/ITINERARY.md the roster reading refreshed and the nib pinned in this round's own commit
recommend check-in (Claude) Tablecloth's other bounds are the mechanical continuation -- max_name=48, max_content_bytes tracking beading.max_resin_bytes, and the eight ClothError paths each want their own pedestal on this same compare-never-copy shape, and each is a lap rather than a question. Two doors still stand above my hand: %328's seat, where the roster's own witness reds whenever the live run card holds any red, so it cannot be rostered while five reds stand -- a design question about what a self-witness may read; and the elder Tend witnesses beside mine, twelve of which still pin their bound a third time inside the guard, where converting them touches Dream's Caravan and Tally rooms and wants his word before a file of his is read against a new shape.
